{"name":"Lava Cake","hex":"#5a4239","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lava cake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of chocolate cake with runny liquid chocolate inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lava_cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Molten chocolate cake","blocks":[{"text":"Molten chocolate cake or runny core cake, is a French dessert that consists of a chocolate cake with a liquid chocolate core. It is named for its molten center, and it is also known as mi-cuit au chocolat, chocolat coulant (\"flowing\"), chocolate lava cake, chocolate fondant, or simply lava cake. It should not be confused with fondant au chocolat, a recipe that contains little flour, but much chocolate and butter, hence melting on the palate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Chocolate_Fondant.jpg/330px-Chocolate_Fondant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molten_chocolate_cake","wikidata":"Q3075365"},{"title":"Lava","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is magma that has been expelled from the interior of a terrestrial planet or a moon onto its surface. Lava may be erupted at a volcano or through a fracture in the crust, on land or underwater, usually at temperatures from 800 to 1,200 °C. Lava may be erupted directly onto the land surface or onto the sea floor or it may be ejected into the atmosphere before falling back down. The solid volcanic rock resulting from subsequent cooling of the molten material is often also called lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-001_Volcano_eruption_of_Litli-Hr%C3%BAtur_in_Iceland_in_2023_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava","wikidata":"Q40157"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"},{"title":"Lava (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lava is a color that is a purplish shade of red. It is named after the color of volcanic lava."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Pahoeoe_fountain_edit2.jpg/330px-Pahoeoe_fountain_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava_(color)","wikidata":"Q6502169"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg/500px-Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg/1280px-Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg/500px-Chocolate_lava_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate lava cake smothered in chocolate sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_lava_cake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/PahoehoeLava.jpg/330px-PahoehoeLava.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia